1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Kernel optimization spends a lot of time waiting for reasoning to finish.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
SpecGen watches the reasoning stream for useful design decisions.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A shared reasoning prefix becomes the starting point for new candidates.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Fast, non-reasoning generations produce kernels while the main stream continues.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Validate correctness first. Profile only the kernels that pass.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
A candidate beats the historical mean. The main generation can stop early.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Feedback goes to the next iteration. If no candidate qualifies, the main path remains.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
An elastic GPU pool adapts at iteration boundaries to keep work moving.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Shared prefix caches reuse the work already done by the model.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Less waiting. More feedback. Better kernels. Read the SpecGen paper.
